skills/external-review/SKILL.md:10:**Bridge command.** `external-reviewer` is the global canonical review-chain bridge command. It is installed by `skills/external-review/install.sh` and delegates to `skills/external-review/scripts/external-reviewer.py` in the active Superstar checkout. Local publish scripts maintain stable materialized plugin-cache entrypoints at `~/.codex/plugins/cache/superstar-dev/superstar/current/` and `~/.claude/plugins/cache/superstar-dev/superstar/current/`; when the installer is run from one of those caches, or when a publisher supplies `EXTERNAL_REVIEWER_SOURCE_ROOT`, the generated shim points at `current/` instead of a versioned cache directory. When the source script is under `$HOME`, the generated shim stores a literal `$HOME/...` path so it does not pin a machine-specific `/home/simon/...` string while still expanding to the checkout at runtime. Do not run or copy a full repo-local `scripts/external-reviewer.py` bridge. Existing repos may keep a tiny compatibility shim at that path only so old handoffs continue to delegate to the global command.
